    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). **Jackson Merrill** is our premier play, benefiting from a soft matchup against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez and a slow delivery that significantly boosts his stolen base upside\u2014a critical factor for our strategy. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** thrives on a favorable wind forecast and a distinct platoon advantage against Michael Lorenzen. While **Nasim Nunez** (71.66) and **Jacob Wilson** (65.19) carry lower base projections, both capitalize on their specific matchup conditions to slot firmly into our starting nine as efficient producers.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the rain risk affecting the game involving **Curtis Mead**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, and **Cole Carrigg**; should that 33% threat manifest, our floor could collapse quickly. Despite the high scores for our starters, **Gunnar Henderson** (58.32) remains the most notable bench casualty. While **Gunnar Henderson** offers elite raw talent, the combination of a sub-4.00 xERA from Eduardo Rivera and a difficult platoon split pushed him just outside our optimal efficiency window today. We are also monitoring **Kyle Tucker** (57.32), whose score is suppressed by Zack Wheeler's elite arm, but his base metrics are too strong to sit, even in a challenging matchup. Note that all projections rely on pending lineups; any shifts in batting order, particularly for **Drake Baldwin** or **Sam Antonacci**, could necessitate a re-evaluation of these efficiency scores before first pitch.",
